course: dictionary
lesson: 10872
title: Same word, different viewing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. The word viewing is like this. «Every Saturday the kids race to tidy their rooms before strangers come for a viewing.» Tidying rooms before strangers arrive means a visit to look round a house, so a viewing is a visit like that.
explain: «An estate agent helps sell houses, and viewings are when people who might buy come to look round.» The clues are estate agent, sell houses and people who might buy. Those words all point to a house, so you can check your guess: a viewing is a time when people look round a house they might buy.
explain: Viewing can also mean watching a film or TV programme, as in family viewing. It can also mean a time before a funeral when people come to see the person who has died and say goodbye. To pick the right meaning, look at the words around it: a house, a screen, or a funeral.
fact: Viewing is the -ing form of the verb view, which means looking at something.
fact: A viewing can be a visit to look round a house or flat you might buy or rent.
fact: Viewing can mean watching TV or films, as in «family viewing».
fact: A funeral viewing is a time before a funeral when people say goodbye to the person who has died.
fact: A viewing platform is a raised place where you can watch birds or the stars.
exercise: «An estate agent helps sell houses, and viewings are when people who might buy come to look round.» What is a viewing here? | A school trip to a castle | *A visit to look round a house you might buy | A time for watching cartoons | A test of how well you can draw
exercise: Mum says the TV guide shows «family viewing» at eight o'clock. What does viewing mean here? | *Watching TV or films together | A raised place for watching birds | A visit to look round a house | A time to say goodbye
exercise: In «Every Saturday the kids race to tidy their rooms before strangers come for a viewing», which word is a clue that the viewing is at a home? | Strangers | Kids | *Rooms | Saturday
test: «Essential viewing» on a sign means something you should watch. What does viewing mean in that phrase? | Buying something | *Watching something | Falling asleep | Singing loudly
test: Viewing is the -ing form of view. What does the verb view mean? | *To look at something | To sing loudly | To be very tired | To buy something
exam: What is a viewing platform? | A room for sleeping | A shelf for books | A car park for buses | *A raised place for watching birds or the stars
